# Mirror Gallery's ruling: "If all Mirror Galleries leave the battlefield, the 'legend rule' will apply the next time
# state-based actions are performed." With the Gallery out, Bot1's Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer and the Clone copying it both
# stay (turn 3). On turn 5 Bot1 casts Disenchant at the Gallery; once it is destroyed the state-based actions find two
# legendary Ragavans under Bot1 (CR 704.5j), and Bot1 chooses which to keep - the second, the Clone - so the Ragavan card
# goes to its owner's graveyard (not destroyed), on top of Disenchant, which went there as the last step of its resolution
# after the Gallery (CR 608.2n), before the state-based actions were checked.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Sol Ring
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer
Mirror Gallery
Clone
Disenchant
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

